testapp,file dialogs — open / folder / save,🔨,✅,🔨,-,-,-,P18,"built on both platforms; not yet clicked on either -- STALE as of 2026-08-28. GTK/Windows went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28, the first time a file dialog was clicked on ANY platform. actions/win/P18-three-dialogs.csv drives all three: each opens a native Windows picker, Escape closes it, and all three result lines read cancelled. Escape rather than a Cancel click because the picker is its own top-level window, not addressable from P18 frame coordinates. The Open/Select/Save path is still untested -- confirming a real selection would mean writing to this machine."
filedialog,gtk_file_dialog_open — single file,✅,✅,➖,-,-,-,P18,run under XWayland only; never on Wayland
filedialog,gtk_file_dialog_open_multiple,⛔,⛔,➖,-,-,-,none,PresentSingleFileOpenDialogAction hardcodes allowMultipleSelections false so no app can reach it
feature,Sheets,✅,✅,⛔,-,-,-,P1,"WinUI does not declare Sheets; P1 covers the WinUI side only. GTK/Windows went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28: P1 driven to open its root sheet, which presents as its own top-level window with the app's green background and rounded corners, both buttons legible. Two things seen while doing it: the red bar does not reach the sheet's content edge, so #660's padding is present on GTK too and not only on WinUI; and the 1px grey border updateSheet draws unconditionally is NOT the same class as the styling overrides fixed that day -- a sheet is presented with isDecorated = false, so the border stands in for decoration the backend removed rather than overriding one the theme supplied. Left alone deliberately"
feature,PopoverMenus,➖,➖,➖,-,-,-,P19 P20,not a capability — one of two ways to implement menus. Gtk uses this one. Earlier rows here framed it as WinUI lacking a feature which was wrong
feature,AttachedMenus,➖,➖,➖,-,-,-,P19 P20,the other way. WinUI uses this one. A backend conforms to exactly one and menuImplementationStyle selects
feature,RevealFiles,⚠️,⚠️,⛔,-,-,-,none,
feature,Alerts,⚠️,⚠️,⛔,-,-,-,P5,WinUI does not declare Alerts; P5 covers the WinUI side only
feature,FileDialogs,🔨,✅,🔨,-,-,-,P18,"GTK/Windows went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28, the first time a file dialog was clicked on ANY platform. actions/win/P18-three-dialogs.csv drives all three: each opens a native Windows picker, Escape closes it, and all three result lines read cancelled. Escape rather than a Cancel click because the picker is its own top-level window, not addressable from P18 frame coordinates. The Open/Select/Save path is still untested -- confirming a real selection would mean writing to this machine."
feature,DatePickers,⚠️,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P11,only covered on AppKit
feature,Windowing / Colors / Paths / Tooltips / Gestures / CornerRadius / gradients,⚠️,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,scattered,no single app compares these
testapp,flat menu — one level with every MenuItem kind,🔨,✅,⚠️,-,-,-,P19,"built on Linux; Windows build not completed yet; nobody has opened the menu -- ALL THREE CLAUSES STALE as of 2026-08-29, and the Windows column had been ➖ (not applicable) while the note said the build was merely unfinished, which is a contradiction on its own. GTK/Windows is ✅: P19-open-and-select.csv already existed and passes -- last action -> second button item and toggle item -> true, so Button, Toggle and the second Button all work and the toggle state reaches the app. P19-menu-open.csv added the half nothing covered, the rendering of the kinds that have no click and no readout: the Text item renders dimmed, and the Divider is a full-width line one row tall, rgb(35,35,35) against the rgb(45,45,45) menu background, measured at two different window positions. gtk_linux still 🔨"
testapp,nested menus — three levels with an item at each,✅,➖,⚠️,-,-,-,P20,"driven under XWayland 2026-08-20: menu opens attached below the button, all four item kinds render including the separator, clicking Button item registers as last action -> button item, and the menu closes on selection"
feature,menu style — AttachedMenus against PopoverMenus,⚠️,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P19 P20,two implementations of one feature not a capability gap; the app cannot choose so the backend decides. Split by menu shape instead: flat in P19 nested in P20
testapp,input controls — Button / Toggle / ToggleSwitch / ToggleButton / Checkbox / Slider / ProgressView / TextField / SecureField / TextEditor,✅,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P21,"widest surface; disabled and indeterminate states usually differ. ToggleSwitch ToggleButton and Checkbox appear in no test app at all -- that clause is STALE, P21 carries all three now. WSL went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28 by reconciliation, NOT a new run: this row still said built-never-executed while another row already recorded the app driven on Linux. See 'input controls driven -- enabled against disabled' and 'P21 test plan run -- slider disabled check'. Remaining gaps keep their own rows: 'P21 steps 6-7 blocked by window height tooling limit' and 'HStack squeezes its first child'"
testapp,text styles — size scale / wrapping / alignment,✅,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P22,"font metrics are the measuring stick for other layout comparisons. WSL went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28 by reconciliation, NOT a new run: this row still said built-never-executed while another row already recorded the app driven on Linux. See 'P22 test plan run -- Narrower/Wider and alignment'. Remaining gap keeps its own row: 'P22 reports two sizes per sample, one degenerate'"
testapp,column view — Table / TableColumn,✅,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P23,"neither type appears in any test app; column widths and selection never compared -- STALE, P23 is that app. WSL went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28 by reconciliation, NOT a new run: this row still said built-never-executed while another row already recorded the app driven on Linux. See 'Table / TableColumn on GtkBackend -- implemented' and 'P23 Fewer rows recovery'. Remaining gap keeps its own row: 'P23 More rows past window height'"
testapp,navigation stack — NavigationStack / NavigationLink,✅,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P24,"neither appears in any test app -- STALE, P24 is that app. P7 and P16 cover NavigationSplitView which is a different type, and that part still holds. WSL went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28 by reconciliation, NOT a new run: this row still said built-never-executed while another row already recorded the app driven on Linux. See 'navigation stack driven'"
proposed,WebView,⚠️,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,none,appears in no test app; no proposal yet because it is unclear what a cross-backend comparison of it would assert
testapp,ContentUnavailableView,🔨,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,P21,appears in no test app; small surface so it could fold into P21 rather than get its own
gap,GtkBackend library target on Windows,➖,✅,➖,-,-,-,none,swift build --target GtkBackend exits 0 — this is the library only
gap,any Pn.exe linked against GtkBackend on Windows,➖,✅,➖,-,-,-,P0 P6-v2,"P0.exe and P6-v2.exe link GtkBackend and no WinUI at all; verified with a symbol scan — 2488 GtkBackend, 0 WinUIBackend"
gap,GtkBackend runtime on Windows,➖,✅,➖,-,-,-,P6-v2,"window opens and renders on Windows for P18 and P6-v2; P19-P24 start and never create one, tracked separately"
gap,compile.zsh -gtk4 on Windows,✅,✅,➖,-,-,-,P0 P6-v2,"needed two fixes: export PKG_CONFIG_PATH so SwiftPM resolves CGtk, and export SCUI_DEFAULT_BACKEND plus drop the WinUI products so the app actually uses Gtk"
gap,compile.zsh -gtk4 on Linux,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P18,verified at 8.31s
gap,file chooser on Wayland after the GtkFileDialog migration,⚠️,➖,➖,-,-,-,P18,the original bug was Wayland-only and the migration is verified on XWayland only
gap,Chinese paths through g_file_get_path on Windows,➖,⚠️,➖,-,-,-,none,reasoned from GLib using UTF-8 rather than measured; the test media filename would expose a fault
gap,incremental build time — Gtk against WinUI on Windows,➖,⚠️,⚠️,-,-,-,none,"full build measured 2026-08-20 on P0: 788s with WinUI against 115s GTK-only, 342 MB against 73 MB. Incremental still unmeasured — that is the number that matters day to day"
testapp,video playback on GtkBackend — decode / present / fps / dropped frames,🔨,✅,➖,-,-,-,P6-v2,"P6 stays WinUI/D3D11 and -gtk4 refuses to build it; P6-v2 is the GTK counterpart. Windows run observed: window renders, video plays, decode d3d11va, present memory-texture (CPU), 30-43 fps at 1080p60"
gap,"GPU presentation on GtkBackend — NV12 over the pipe, converted in a shader",🔨,✅,➖,-,-,-,P6-v2,done: Gtk.NV12GLView uploads NV12 as two textures and converts in a fragment shader. 1080p60 went 23-43 fps to 51.9 with read 19-32ms to 8.55ms. Not a backend-agnostic API yet — the app still writes its own GtkWidgetRepresentable
gap,zero-copy decode to GL on Windows — D3D11 texture imported as a GL texture,➖,⚠️,➖,-,-,-,none,still open and distinct from row 55. NV12+GL cut the transport 2.7x but frames still cross CPU memory through the ffmpeg pipe. True zero-copy needs in-process decode plus glImportMemoryWin32HandleEXT; external-objects-win32 is confirmed present on this machine
gap,GTK layout warnings — GtkFixed measure and allocation,⚠️,⚠️,➖,-,-,-,P0 P6-v2,"the measure-before-allocate warning is fixed in gtk_custom_root_widget.c and gone for every app. The remaining `Allocation height too small` is a real report of a real condition — the window is smaller than its content — and P0 still fires it 875 times in 25s. Silencing it by allocating the child minimum would hide that, so it is left"
gap,"P7-P24 on Windows/GtkBackend, verified one at a time",✅,✅,✅,-,-,-,P7-P24,"13 of 15 open their window: P7 P8 P9 P10 P12 P13 P14 P15 P16 P18 P19 P20 P21 P22 P24. Only P11 and P23 failed, both for named reasons, both fixed or tracked. The earlier claim that P19-P24 were a Windows-specific failure was a harness fault and is retracted; apps must be launched one at a time from a correct POSIX environment"
gap,Table / TableColumn on GtkBackend — implemented,✅,✅,✅,-,-,-,P23,"Gtk.Table: a GtkGrid inside a GtkScrolledWindow, headers in row 0, cells from row 1, rebuilt on each setCells like AppKit's reloadData. Driven under XWayland: renders four columns and eight rows, and answers its own question — the long cell in row 3 is truncated rather than widening its column"
testapp,P7 P8 P9 P10 P13 P15 P16 P17 P18 under XWayland,✅,⚠️,✅,-,-,-,many,"all nine opened a window and rendered on Linux/GtkBackend, driven by drive_xdotool.zsh 2026-08-20. Windows: P7 verified working from a correct environment; P8-P16 exit immediately and are under investigation; P17's exe is a stale WinUI build and proves nothing about GtkBackend"
gap,assertionFailure on an unsupported style is fatal on Windows and silent on Linux,✅,✅,➖,-,-,-,P11,"P11 asked for .datePickerStyle(.compact); GtkBackend supports only [.automatic .graphical] and DatePickerStyleModifier calls assertionFailure before falling back. Assertions trap in debug and vanish in release, and this project builds debug on Windows and release on Linux — so the same code on the same backend was fatal on one platform only. Fixed in P11 by reading Environment supportedDatePickerStyles first"
testapp,nested menus driven — three levels under XWayland,✅,✅,✅,-,-,-,P20,"level 1 opens, Level 2 submenu opens on click and level 3 is reachable. GTK PopoverMenu navigates by sliding with a back chevron rather than cascading, which is the PopoverMenus against AttachedMenus difference this app exists to show. Windows/GTK went 🔨 -> ✅ on 2026-08-28, driven through the InputEvent harness rather than xdotool: the menu opens, a disabled item is dimmed rgb(145,145,144) against rgb(238,238,236), and clicking it does nothing while the next click reaches Level 1 item. The earlier note said ""Windows built but not yet driven — no xdotool there"", which stopped being the reason once Win32Synthesiser existed"
testapp,drive_xdotool.zsh can click,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,none,"--click X,Y --key KEYS --pause SECS, each step capturing its own numbered screenshot. Before this the driver only launched an app and captured its initial state, so no control in any Pn had ever been operated"
testapp,input controls driven — enabled against disabled,✅,🔨,✅,-,-,-,P21,"clicks reads 1 after clicking Enabled then Disabled, so the disabled button refuses input rather than only looking disabled. Defect found: the ToggleSwitch and Checkbox rows truncate their Enabled labels to ... and En..."
testapp,navigation stack driven,✅,🔨,✅,-,-,-,P24,"two pushes take it from Level 0 to Level 2 and the button becomes Push level 3. pushes recorded stays 0 because only the Record a push button feeds it, which is how the app is written"
gap,HStack squeezes its first child — toggle labels truncate,⚠️,⚠️,➖,-,-,-,P21,"in P21 the .switch row shows Enabled as ... and the .checkbox row as En..., while Disabled beside it renders in full. The first child of the HStack is not given its natural width. Observed on Linux/GtkBackend under XWayland 2026-08-20; Windows not yet compared"
testapp,full Pn sweep on Linux/GtkBackend,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P0-P24 P6-v2,"all 26 build, open a window and reach their first frame with no fatal error, run one at a time under XWayland 2026-08-20. This is a smoke test, not the test plan: the plan carries about 190 numbered steps and roughly 10 have been executed"
testapp,P17 test plan run — the numbers it exists to produce,✅,⚠️,✅,-,-,-,P17,"first actual run of P17s steps, Linux/GtkBackend 2026-08-20. #264 fixedSize does NOT reproduce: subject 160x16 against control 372x16, so the ideal width reached fixedSize. #161: the picker is sized from the selected item, width moving 42 to 51 to 154 to 392 as longer items are chosen. #266b DOES reproduce: the three coloured bands do not end up the same width. Windows side not yet run"
gap,#266b — ideal-width VStack bands not equal,⛔,⚠️,✅,-,-,-,P17,the three coloured bands in P17s last section render at different widths on GtkBackend when the plan requires them equal. Reproduces the upstream issue rather than being new. Fixing it is SwiftCrossUI VStack layout work
gap,#158 — Group inside ZStack stacks vertically instead of overlapping,⛔,⚠️,✅,-,-,-,P13,P13 step 5. The red green and blue rectangles appear one below another with no overlap. Clearest of the three container defects because the intended behaviour is unambiguous. See testapp/gtk-test-plan-findings.md
gap,"P22 reports two sizes per sample, one degenerate",⚠️,⚠️,➖,-,-,-,P22,"each of the eight font samples reports both a plausible measurement and a vertical-strip one, e.g. 185x13 alongside 15x397. Rendering is correct but the app exists to compare reported widths, and two contradictory numbers leave nothing to compare"
testapp,P0 test plan run -- all 9 steps,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P0,AppStorage increment/reset/relaunch persistence and both AlertScene/environment-alert paths all pass under XWayland with no crash. AlertScene renders as a second undecorated untitled top-level window sized to content (202x60) not captured by name-filtered window lists
testapp,P1 test plan run -- all 11 steps,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P1,open/folder/save GtkFileDialog all appear within 1s of the click (#523 stays fixed); root sheet padding stays removed (#660); nested sheet opens and dismisses independently of the root sheet (#659). Each dialog/sheet is its own top-level window found by diffing the window list
testapp,P2 test plan run -- Picker and TextEditor steps,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P2,"Picker option-list update (#449) and TextEditor typing/no-border (#471) both pass. Picker dropdown is its own top-level window, 122x94 for 2 options growing to 128x190 for 5"
gap,P2 disabled-button visual distinction (#390),⚠️,✅,✅,-,-,-,"P2, P21","RESOLVED 2026-08-28, by measuring P21 rather than P2 -- P21 puts an enabled and a disabled control side by side, which is the comparison P2 could not make. GTK/Windows passes: enabled label rgb(238,238,236) against disabled rgb(99,99,98). WinUI/Windows was genuinely broken and is fixed in 757e6d1c -- both labels were rgb(255,255,255) and the two buttons differed only by a 3-unit fill (45 vs 42); disabled is now rgb(120,120,120). The cause was apply(to:) writing a foreground brush onto the Button's child TextBlock, which does not inherit the ContentPresenter's disabled Foreground. gtk_linux still untested. EARLIER NOTE KEPT, because it is a good record of what a plausible dead end looks like -- it treated a tooling limit as an open question about the feature: inconclusive not a pass or a fail: the two disabled controls have no observable side effect besides their own look, so only a screenshot is available. A border seen on the enabled control at cold launch disappears after any click and never reappears, consistent with either a one-time focus ring (meaning no real distinction exists once focus moves, a #390 regression) or with the enabling click never reaching the state binding (meaning nothing was actually compared). Needs an app change to resolve"
gap,P2 window resize disabled -- full screen button (#401),⚠️,➖,➖,-,-,-,P2,"not usefully testable with xdotool: windowsize issues a raw X ConfigureWindow request and resized the window 620x643 to 900x700 even with windowResizable=false, but that is not the same thing as a user dragging an edge or pressing a maximize button, and no maximize button was confirmed present in this XWayland session at all"
gap,P3 three-column initial layout regression,✅,➖,✅,-,-,-,P3,"REGRESSION reproduces and is worse than documented: sidebar/middle List content (headers, Split layout, Details, Detail B, Detail C rows) is largely absent at launch, not merely mis-sized, and unlike the tracked (Fixed) bug it does NOT self-correct on Force state update or on a window resize to 1100x700 -- pixel-identical before/after both"
gap,#389 image clipping,✅,➖,✅,-,-,-,P3,reproduces at Large (2.4x scale): image overflows its 220x140 frame far enough to reach the 960px window edge. Small (1.0x) stays clean inside the frame
testapp,P3 test plan run -- all 8 testable steps,⚠️,➖,➖,-,-,-,P3,see the two gap rows above for the two failures found; Small/Medium/Large buttons themselves respond correctly
testapp,P4 test plan run -- callback-storage steps,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P4,"#190 callback storage passes: Run N buttons, Force update, More/Fewer rows, Rows 250 + Run last all track callbacks/Selected row correctly across row-count changes. Native banner steps (2-4) are n/a by design on GTK (WinUIBackend-only #else branch). Scroll-slide step (9) not tested, no scroll-wheel step in drive_xdotool.zsh"
testapp,P5 test plan run -- cross-window half,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P5,"#675 cross-window half stays fixed: Alert A on main and Alert A on secondary coexist simultaneously, second does not wait for first to close"
gap,#675 same-window alert stacking,✅,➖,✅,-,-,-,P5,"REGRESSION: cannot be reached through the UI at all on GtkBackend. The first alert is an application-modal Gtk.MessageDialog that blocks all further input to its parent window, so clicking Show Alert B/C while an alert is already showing on that window is a no-op (status text unchanged, no new window). Verified the button coordinate is correct via a sanity click with no alert open. Steps 7-13 of P5 could not be exercised as a result"
gap,P7 near-total render failure (sidebar/detail/list content missing),⛔,➖,➖,-,-,-,P7,"SEVERE regression, worse than #556 as tracked: window shows only a ~37x35 bordered box, no list rows, no status text, no buttons, unchanged after a 2s settle pause and after resizing to 900x600. p7-debug-events.log (from the split views own measurement probes, --debug) stayed empty across 3 launches including a 10s wait, meaning sidebar/detail/total panes were never measured -- consistent with the split view collapsing to near-nothing. p7-startup.log confirms App.init/App.body/RootView.body all run normally, so this is a rendering/layout failure downstream of view-tree construction, not a startup crash"
testapp,P7 test plan run -- steps 2-8,⛔,➖,➖,-,-,-,P7,"could not be meaningfully evaluated: no visible List, status line, or split divider to check against, see the gap row above"
testapp,P8 test plan run -- #417 corner radius,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P8,"does not reproduce: the red block corners are visibly rounded, matching cornerRadius(20). RENDER COMPLETE marker confirms all probes measured, unlike P7"
gap,#426 scroll-wheel test tooling,⚠️,➖,➖,-,-,-,P8,"could not be exercised: xdotool click --window WID 5 (wheel down) produced no change even as a control scrolled over plain scrollable content, so the input method itself is not reaching the ScrolledWindow via this tool. drive_xdotool.zsh only issues button-1 clicks. Needs a different scroll-simulation approach before this step can be run"
testapp,P9 test plan run -- all steps,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P9,"neither #504 nor #295 reproduces: field heights unchanged across 3x Force update; text stays inside the blue frame band at 200px, narrower, zero width (0 px, text visibly does not spill), and back to 200px wide"
gap,#454 transparent overlay consumes clicks,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P10,"reproduces: Covered clicks stayed 0 with the overlay present, then registered (1) immediately once the overlay was unchecked -- same button, same click, isolates the overlay as the cause"
gap,#478 Ctrl-Q does not quit,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P10,reproduces: window still present in the window list after xdotool key ctrl+q
testapp,P10 test plan run -- all steps,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P10,see the two gap rows above; Direct clicks counter itself works correctly (2 clicks -> Direct clicks: 2)
gap,#386 GTK dark mode text colour,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P15,"does NOT reproduce as described: with GTK_THEME=Adwaita:dark, Plain text on the default background renders light-coloured and legible, not unreadable dark-on-dark. Requested/Resolved override confirmed still ignored (Resolved stays light regardless of System/Light/Dark presses), which is the separate, expected-by-design half. Worth a maintainer re-check since this contradicts the Open tracking"
gap,#289 window minimum height vs CSD title bar,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P15,"reproduces and gets WORSE after growing content: before interacting, xdotool windowsize could not force the window below ~472-560px (some minimum was enforced). After clicking Use tall content (confirmed via button label flip and 6 new rows appearing), the identical resize call that was refused now succeeds completely, dropping the window to 100px and clipping everything past the second line of text. Minimum height enforcement is lost rather than growing with content"
testapp,P15 test plan run -- all testable steps,⚠️,➖,➖,-,-,-,P15,"see the two gap rows above; Content area readout (300 x 24) never updates across short/tall content or resize, noted but not chased further"
testapp,P16 test plan run -- GtkBackend control for #160,✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P16,"correct from the first stable frame: sidebar 180x22, detail 660x22, both before and after Force update, no jump to compare. #160 is WinUIBackend-specific and does not apply on GTK. 3-column layout (step 7) and relaunch+resize (step 6) not tried this sweep"
filedialog,gtk_file_dialog_select_folder,✅,✅,➖,-,-,-,P18,driven under XWayland: Choose a folder then Cancel closes the dialog and reports folder -> cancelled
filedialog,gtk_file_dialog_save,✅,✅,➖,-,-,-,P18,"driven under XWayland: Choose a save destination opens with Name prefilled exactly p18-example.txt, confirming the only path exercising set_initial_name"
testapp,P21 test plan run -- slider disabled check (step 5),✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P21,pass: dragging the enabled slider moved it 0.40 to 0.88; the same drag on the disabled slider directly below left it unchanged
gap,P21 steps 6-7 blocked by window height tooling limit,⛔,➖,➖,-,-,-,P21,TextField/SecureField/TextEditor disabled comparison and ContentUnavailableView are below the visible frame in a plain VStack (no ScrollView). xdotool windowsize clamps at the screen height (1080px) regardless of requested value; moving the window off-screen first did not lift the clamp. Same root tooling gap as the P8 scroll-wheel limitation
testapp,P22 test plan run -- Narrower/Wider and alignment (steps 3-4),✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P22,pass: 150pt wraps the sample sentence cleanly into five lines with no overflow; leading/center/trailing land at expected positions in the 320pt frame
gap,P23 More rows past window height (step 3),⚠️,➖,➖,-,-,-,P23,observed as clipping rather than scrolling: going from 8 to 24 rows leaves row 13 cut mid-line at the window bottom with no visible scrollbar and rows 14-24 unreachable in the captured frame. Not fully confirmed a scrollbar is genuinely absent versus just not rendered -- same scroll-testing tooling gap noted for P8/P21
testapp,P23 Fewer rows recovery (step 4),✅,➖,➖,-,-,-,P23,"pass: back to rows: 1 shows one clean row, no leftover gap or stale row"
gap,RETRACTED — P7 near-total render failure was a self-inflicted regression,✅,⚠️,✅,-,-,-,P7,"a startup trace added to P7RootView.body during this session blanked the window: a statement before an explicit return in a result-builder property. Reported as a severe backend defect, traced to the trace itself. P7.swift restored; it renders lists, split view and buttons correctly. The same pattern was in P11 and is removed there too"
feature,"Compositing effects: opacity, blur, saturation, brightness, contrast, grayscale, hueRotation",🔨,✅,⚠️,-,-,-,P39,"BackendFeatures.VisualEffects, new 2026-08-27. GtkBackend does all seven, verified on Windows against an identity control in the same window. WinUIBackend applies opacity only and logs the six it drops -- it needs a Microsoft.UI.Composition effect graph. gtk_linux is built but the app was not run there"
feature,"Geometric effects: offset, rotationEffect, scaleEffect, transformEffect",⛔,⛔,✅,-,-,-,P40,"BackendFeatures.GeometricEffects, new 2026-08-27. WinUIBackend renders all of them correctly. GtkBackend conforms and deliberately applies nothing: GTK 4.22.4 draws any transformed widget as flat hotpink rgb(255,105,180), GSK's indicator for a node it cannot render, losing the content entirely. See bugs/Gtk4-bugs.md. gtk_linux marked blocked by inference from the same version, not measured"
gap,backend styling overrides the platform theme instead of suggesting a default,-,✅,⚠️,⚠️,⚠️,-,"P2, P9, P20, P21, P29","GtkBackend installed per-widget CSS at GTK_STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_APPLICATION (600, above THEME 200), so no theme or style class could restyle any control it had touched; three call sites had already worked around it one at a time. Fixed a593b3c9 and 10e7bead: both the shared cssProperties block and the popover menu now stand down when the theme already draws the requested scheme. WinUI foreground fixed 757e6d1c; still open there are table cell text, the combo box black default, and TextControlBorderBrushFocused set fully transparent, which unlike the GTK case has no outline fallback. AppKit and UIKit pin .foregroundColor into attributedTitle so isEnabled does not dim the label -- code-read only, needs a Mac. Protocol root cause: suggestedForegroundColor is never nil, so a backend cannot tell an explicit colour from no preference; documented on it a593b3c9"
